.TH GOCAT-TUNNEL 1 "December 2024" "GoCat 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gocat-tunnel \- SSH tunneling
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gocat tunnel
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create SSH tunnels for local, remote, and dynamic port forwarding.
Supports SOCKS proxy mode for dynamic tunneling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-ssh " " \fIUSER@HOST\fR
SSH server to connect to
.TP
.BR \-\-local " " \fIPORT\fR
Local port for forwarding
.TP
.BR \-\-remote " " \fIHOST:PORT\fR
Remote host and port
.TP
.BR \-\-reverse
Enable reverse (remote) port forwarding
.TP
.BR \-\-dynamic " " \fIPORT\fR
Enable dynamic SOCKS proxy on port
.TP
.BR \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
SSH private key file
.TP
.BR \-\-password
Prompt for password authentication
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Local port forwarding:
.B gocat tunnel --ssh user@server --local 8080 --remote localhost:80
.TP
Remote port forwarding:
.B gocat tunnel --ssh user@server --reverse --local 3000 --remote 8080
.TP
Dynamic SOCKS proxy:
.B gocat tunnel --ssh user@server --dynamic 1080
.TP
With SSH key:
.B gocat tunnel --ssh user@server --key ~/.ssh/id_rsa --local 8080 --remote 80
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gocat (1),
.BR ssh (1)
